# Contentful Delivery API — the build's data source (AWK-39, ADR-0002).
#
# Copy to `.env` and fill in the token. `.env` is gitignored; this file is not,
# which is the whole point of it: the NAMES are the thing that has to be right,
# and reading a name the Netlify dashboard does not hold fails by rendering an
# EMPTY SITE rather than by erroring.
#
# These three are set in the Netlify UI, never in netlify.toml, which is
# committed. Verified against the dashboard on 2026-08-15:
#
#   CONTENTFUL_SPACE_ID          all scopes, same value in all deploy contexts
#   CONTENTFUL_ENVIRONMENT       all scopes, same value in all deploy contexts
#   CONTENTFUL_DELIVERY_TOKEN    Builds, Functions and Runtime — and FOUR values
#                                across four deploy contexts, unlike the other
#                                two. So a context whose token is empty or wrong
#                                builds a site with no content and exits 0.
#                                app/lib/contentful.ts asserts all three are
#                                present and non-empty so that fails loudly.
#
# NOT the CMA token. `CONTENTFUL_CMA_TOKEN` (CFPAT-…) is write access, is read
# only by the scripts under scripts/contentful/, and must never enter CI — it
# stays local in ~/.contentful-cma-token.
#
# One spelling trap: scripts/contentful/import_to_contentful.py reads
# CONTENTFUL_ENVIRONMENT_ID, with the _ID. The build reads CONTENTFUL_ENVIRONMENT
# per ADR-0002 and netlify.toml. Both spellings are live in this repo.

CONTENTFUL_SPACE_ID=3iiyvj5u5c9h
CONTENTFUL_ENVIRONMENT=master
CONTENTFUL_DELIVERY_TOKEN=
